---
import Avatar from './Avatar.astro';
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';

const chips = ['A landing page', 'A launch plan', 'A researched report'];
const criteria = [
  ['AC-1', 'The menu shows every drink with its price'],
  ['AC-2', 'Opening hours read right on any phone'],
  ['AC-3', 'Order ahead, pay at pickup'],
];
---

<section id="how" class="relative z-10 mx-auto mt-32 max-w-6xl scroll-mt-8 px-4 sm:px-6">
  <SectionHead eyebrow="How it works" title="From one sentence to done.">
    No setup wizard and no prompt writing. Say what you want and the crew takes it from there. You
    approve the plan, and you approve what comes back.
  </SectionHead>

  <ol class="mt-12 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-3xl border border-line bg-panel/60 p-5">
      <span class="font-mono text-xs text-dim">01 · Say it</span>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-raised p-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-white/85">
        A simple website for my coffee cart, with our menu and opening hours
        <span
          aria-hidden="true"
          class="animate-caret ml-0.5 inline-block h-4 w-px translate-y-0.5 bg-white"
        ></span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 text-[11px] text-white/60">
        {chips.map((chip) => (
          <span class="rounded-full border border-line px-2 py-0.5">{chip}</span>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="mt-auto text-sm leading-relaxed text-dim">
        The project, its folder and its crew are made from that one line. Atlas asks what it needs
        to know.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-3xl border border-line bg-panel/60 p-5">
      <span class="font-mono text-xs text-dim">02 · Approve the plan</span>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-black/30 p-3 text-[12px]">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-2 font-medium text-white">
          <Avatar clank="scribe" size="xs" /> Spec v1 · 4 stories
        </span>
        {criteria.map(([key, text]) => (
          <span class="text-dim">
            <span class="font-mono text-accent">{key}</span> {text}
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="mt-auto text-sm leading-relaxed text-dim">
        Scribe writes down what will be made, story by story. Nothing is built until you say yes.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-3xl border border-line bg-panel/60 p-5">
      <span class="font-mono text-xs text-dim">03 · Watch them work</span>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-black/30 p-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-dim">CLK-103</span>
        <span class="text-[13px]">Order ahead for pickup</span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[12px] text-accent-2">
          <Avatar clank="forge" size="xs" live /> Forge · Running npm test
        </span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-auto text-sm leading-relaxed text-dim">
        Tickets land on the board. Several clanks work at once, each on its own copy of the project.
      </p>
    </li>

    <li class="flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-3xl border border-amber-300/20 bg-amber-300/[0.03] p-5">
      <span class="font-mono text-xs text-amber-200/80">04 · You approve</span>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-black/30 p-3 text-[12px]">
        <span class="text-white">CLK-101 · Home page</span>
        <span class="text-dim">Checked by Gauge · Signed off by Atlas</span>
        <span class="mt-1 self-start rounded-full bg-white px-3 py-1 font-medium text-black">
          Approve and merge
        </span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-auto text-sm leading-relaxed text-dim">
        Approving merges the work, on GitHub if that's where the project lives. Nothing ships on a
        drag or a guess.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>
